>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `refute`

``` hol4
Refute.refute : config -> term -> outcome
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample to a term.

`refute cfg tm` closes `tm` universally, runs the backends `cfg`
selects, prints the outcome unless `cfg` is quiet, checks its `expect`
field, and returns the outcome:

``` hol4
datatype outcome =
    Counterexample of counterexample list
  | NoCounterexample
  | Model of counterexample list
  | NoModel
  | Unknown of string list
```

`NoCounterexample` means the whole relevant space was covered;
`Unknown` lists why the search was inconclusive.  `Model` and
`NoModel` answer a model-finder search with the `falsify` field false.
A counterexample's `certainty` is `Genuine`, `QuasiGenuine` or
`Potential`; its `cert` field, when `SOME th`, is a theorem refuting
`tm`.

`refute_with updates tm` is `refute (current_config updates) tm`, and
`refute_def tm` is `refute_with [] tm`.  `quickcheck` and
`model_refute` are `refute_with [upd_search QuickcheckBackends]` and
`refute_with [upd_search (Only [ModelFinder])]`.

### Failure

Fails only if the `expect` field is not met.  Backend failures and
timeouts become `Unknown`.

### Example

>>__ load "Refute";
>> case Refute.refute
          (Refute.default_config
             |> Refute.upd_search (Refute.Only [Refute.Exhaustive])
             |> Refute.upd_size 4
             |> Refute.upd_quiet true)
          ``(n : num) < 3`` of
       Refute.Counterexample (cex :: _) => SOME (#bindings cex)
     | _ => NONE;

